  "notes": "USAGE:\nPrimarily used in formal and institutional contexts such as parliaments, the United Nations, corporate boards, and other deliberative bodies.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {決議|けつぎ}を{採択|さいたく}する (to adopt a resolution)\n- {決議|けつぎ}{案|あん} (draft resolution)\n- {決議|けつぎ}が{可決|かけつ}される (a resolution is passed)\n- {決議|けつぎ}が{否決|ひけつ}される (a resolution is rejected)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {議決|ぎけつ}: parliamentary decision — focuses on the act of deciding by vote in an assembly\n- {決定|けってい}: decision — a broader term for decisions in general, not limited to formal votes",
